References:
No permanent specification is cited at the provisional stage. Per RFC 7595 a citable 
specification is required only for permanent registration; the credible reasons for 
deferring it are (1) reference stability - the name is reserved under FCFS so that 
gdsi URIs already shown as non-normative examples have a stable, unambiguous namespace 
while the defining specification is finalized; and (2) definitional stability - 
permanent registration fixes the scheme's semantics, and the definition's scope is 
still being closed, so a permanent definition would lock in semantics prematurely. 
The registration will be updated to Permanent, with a citable specification, upon publication.